Asbestos Register Upgrade
High-Level Requirements
Item	Detail
Version / status	v1.0, 13 November 2026, draft for review
Author	Victor Peters, Business Analyst, Technology and Digital Solutions
Programme	TOM programme, Workstream 1 (Connecting Data)
Sources	Asbestos Register Requirements Scoping Session, 12 November 2026 (48 min), and the analyst's session notes
Audience	Session attendees and project team
1. Executive summary
Users need a true asbestos register: one clear, consolidated line per room or element for each property. Today they get a list of every survey line ever recorded. Stakeholders called the current data a "treasure hunt": the same lounge ceiling can appear up to 10 to 12 times, older surveys name locations inconsistently, and the surveys behind the data are poorly labelled.
The upgrade will be built on cleansed data in Microsoft Fabric. PIMS stays the master database, and where users will view the register is still to be decided. The session also asked for faster survey and removal updates through automation, clearer alerts, and neater asbestos information for customers.
The biggest open item is the set of rules for merging conflicting survey results. The Asbestos & Compliance Lead will define these.
