5. Current state (as-is)
Asbestos information moves from survey contractors into PIMS by hand and reaches users as one long, unconsolidated list.
1.	A survey is requested (refurbishment, targeted or management). Its status is tracked on a Smartsheet fed by the contractor, now rolled out to Major Repairs.
2.	The contractor (currently Franks Portlock for all new surveys) emails the completed survey to the asbestos inbox.
3.	Survey data is validated by hand, then loaded into PIMS in a weekly bulk upload, so there can be up to a week's delay.
4.	Some teams skip the wait by saving surveys from the email into a house file for operatives.
5.	Users see every line from every survey in the PIMS contractor portal. Positives are highlighted in red, the newest survey shows first, and there are basic filters.
6.	When a removal is completed, the waste consignment note goes to Emma Jorgenson's team, who delete each matching line in PIMS by hand.
7.	Customer letters embed a table pulled straight from PIMS.
The old data warehouse (WhereScape) will be switched off early in 2027 and replaced by Fabric.
